# Run tests after significant changes

Before considering work complete on a coding task, run tests when **any** of these apply:

- Changes under `src/`, `library/`, `interface/`, `modules/`, or `tests/`
- Database or migration changes (`sql/`, Doctrine migrations)
- Dependency or tooling changes (`composer.json`, `composer.lock`, `phpunit.xml*`, `package.json`)
- Refactors touching more than ~3 files in the same feature area
- Public API, routes, or security-sensitive code

**How to run (OpenEMR):**

- Full quality pass from repo root: `composer code-quality` when many PHP files changed
- Isolated tests (no DB): `composer phpunit-isolated`
- In Docker (full suite): from `docker/development-easy/`, `docker compose exec openemr /root/devtools unit-test` (and other devtools targets as appropriate)

Choose the narrowest command that still covers the change. If tests fail, fix or explain the blocker before ending the turn.

If only docs or comments changed, tests are optional unless CI still runs on those paths.
